CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:237:## 7. Milestones and independent exit criteria
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:249:### M2 — Version-aware continuous assurance (B + C)
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:255:**Deliver:** local model adapter, normalized document/query formatting, local vector index, `POST /api/discovery`, proposed-link review workflow, evaluation report against labeled fixtures.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:264:**Ordering:** M0 precedes independent development. M1/M2 do not wait for M3. Start M3 work in parallel after M0, but merge through contracts only.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:311:**Every story is done only when:** acceptance criteria are tested; fixtures cover success and failure; source provenance and revision are preserved when applicable; API examples are updated; tests pass offline; docs include an invocation/demo; code is reviewed. Explicitly document any assumptions in freshness rules.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:313:**Security and correctness:** No secrets in fixtures. Treat indexed repository text as untrusted input. No unreviewed AI result should be promoted to accepted link or verification evidence. Never silently mix embeddings from different models/index versions in one vector collection.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:331:7. **Team workflow:** conventional PR review, one story per PR when practical, and contract changes reviewed by affected owners.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:341:5. Use `AGENTS.md` for repo-specific coding conventions. Prefer small, reviewable patches.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:349:> First inspect the repository and tell me what is actually present. If this is an empty/new repository, implement **Milestone M0 only**: repository scaffold, versioned domain schemas/contracts, a synthetic banking fixture repo with real baseline-a/b Git history and labeled expected outcomes, deterministic fake discovery data, offline tests, and setup documentation. Make sensible small decisions and record them as ADRs. Do not invent external services or claim model inference works without testing it. Then run the tests and report files changed, results, and the three independently assignable follow-on PRs (A-PR1, B-PR1, C-PR1). If the repository already contains work, identify the next incomplete milestone and propose the smallest safe vertical slice before editing.
CONTINUOUS_TRACEABILITY_ROADMAP.md:367:**Definition of project success for the first release:** A reviewer can inspect a reproducible, revision-specific requirement-to-verification thread and distinguish confirmed failures, coverage gaps, potentially stale evidence, and unreviewed semantic suggestions—without depending on a permanently online AI cluster.

